answer:
In part. A Chinese reader gets the same account and the same standings, but only through three front pages. Almost everything else is in English or out of date. On honesty the Chinese side is the strongest part of the repository. On access it is the weakest.

Same account: ONE-PAGE.zh.md and THE-THEORY-OF-BECOMING.zh.md are complete, faithful editions. Both have 198 lines and the same ten sections as the English, with every standing, every [AI 读法] tag, both premises (延续条件 and C) and T8's "不主张对一切可能的心智都有约束力的裁断". The prose, though, is close translation from English (欧化), and the T7 row is a single sentence of about 250 characters. Every link out of these pages leads into English: 八章, 理论图, chapters 01–05, 07 and 08, GLOSSARY, OPENING, ONE-ARGUMENT, COLLECTIVE-DIRECTION and the alignment and philosophy dossiers. On GitHub, README.md's first screen and nav bar have no 中文 link. The first one comes at line 137, after about 9,400 English words, and there is no root README.zh.md.

The relation to the texts is stated honestly, and the two Chinese dossiers are exemplary:
- They list the commentaries not consulted.
- They record textual variants.
- They concede that "理论之续正站在《中论》所破的那一边" (the theory's continuation sits on the side the 中论 refutes).
- They label the 中华本 經 "AI 所撰之仿古文，不是古文" (pseudo-classical text written by AI, not classical text).
- They keep "相合不是印证" (agreement is not confirmation).

Two weaker spots. Chapter 06's thesis words the origin more strongly than the front pages do ("诸定义是从所选古文重构", the definitions are reconstructed from the chosen texts). And README's English gloss "The relational start holds across the lines" goes past chapter 06's own "主导线索" (main thread) and its list of what is not shown.

生生 is shown honestly as T8, an argued thesis, but not clearly as the work's aim. It appears once on ONE-PAGE.zh, in a table cell. 「生生之谓易」 and the two senses in 孔颖达's commentary appear only in chapter 06 and dossier item C-13. Worse, the same characters carry three senses:
- the ethics' 生生;
- the grammar's «生生» and «生生不息» (Lean theorems about renewal without end);
- OPENING's closing line 生生不息.

The warning that these differ sits only in the English GLOSSARY, chapter 01 and deep in chapter 06.

What is missing on the Chinese side:
- a Chinese entry on GitHub;
- Chinese editions of the chapters, GLOSSARY and OPENING (the value statement);
- the 中华本 itself, the one full Chinese statement, which is a 637k-character text dated 10-21 in history/. Chapter 06 §7.3 still presents it in the present tense as "以古名重述全论" (the whole account restated in classical names), and only chapter 06's 未决 list says it must be rewritten;
- the work on Chinese thought (248 passages, 5,673 judgments, the hexagram world), which is in neither overview;
- one fixed Chinese term each: widening appears as 扩大, 广 and 拓宽, and C as 扩大可形成者更好 and 以广为愈.
